{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:05:10.052Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f2b26af0d83e107f5a192eb9d81d71ded2e95d3c5d429aac77e92965c1382dc5","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes. All three notes are public, so you can open them yourself:\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 about gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments not reaching drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18). Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift cleared. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025), `dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday`.\n- **#4419**: Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\", `dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet`. That note has no date, so I can't say when the ticket was logged.\n\nThe other Moss notes I found for QFL (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't carry a ticket number.\n\nI stuck to Moss's notes as you asked. Other QFL ticket numbers exist in non-Moss pages, such as #4912, #4819 and #8841, and I can list those with sources if you want them too. Also, the cheat sheet warns that Quarendon Freightways is a different company, not a Pemberline customer, so those tickets shouldn't be mixed in."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
